# playpick cell: mode=clear spec=shaman:elemental style=melee size=10
# difficulty=normal view=820x1180,touch save=carried.
#
# Checked sessions.jsonl first (every shaman:elemental line, every mode=clear
# line): this spec has three prior clear-mode evenings -- good/25-heroic,
# melee/25-heroic, flee/10-normal/fresh -- but never melee at its own default
# 10-normal tier, and never a carried save on this spec at 10-normal either
# (#273/hypothesis 5: carried behaves as fresh under playbot's per-PID port,
# so this is really a second fresh-profile reading, not a continuation).
#
# What this is actually for: hypothesis 6 (THE VIGIL stalls any evening at a
# fixed point) was opened on 10-normal (druid:guardian, wander/good/flee all
# stalled 250-400s there) and then narrowed toward size/difficulty rather than
# spec/style when shaman:elemental crossed VIGIL clean in ~30s on 25-heroic
# under both good and melee. This cell is the missing cross: the same spec
# that crossed clean at 25-heroic, now at the 10-normal tier where the stall
# was first seen, under melee (not yet tried at 10-normal on any spec). If it
# stalls here, hypothesis 6 is purely about size/difficulty. If it crosses
# clean, spec matters too and the "narrowed by" clause needs another look.
open
tap raid
shot raid-setup
tap next
tap class:shaman:elemental
shot class-selected
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
state
shot start
targets
ui
evening melee 240 10
shot end
state
says
bill
